{"type":"text","timestamp":1794324825642,"sessionID":"ses_e39f40dfaffeJMKs6SiMZ6Mx9w","part":{"id":"prt_1c6180617001zc9T9lafVTJO6W","messageID":"msg_1c6166fe5001WEv7V672N1WHmk","sessionID":"ses_e39f40dfaffeJMKs6SiMZ6Mx9w","type":"text","text":"Found it: pip's `get_requirements` treats hashed constraints as requirements with hash options, which forces `--require-hashes` mode — and then every requirement needs `==` pins + hashes on its own lines. The fix: make `requirements.txt` a complete pinned+hashed set (the standard `--require-hashes` pattern), keeping the Dockerfile's `-r ... -c ...` contract intact. Let me build it from the lock file:","time":{"start":1794324825623,"end":1794324825638}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794324825734,"sessionID":"ses_e39f40dfaffeJMKs6SiMZ6Mx9w","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_9b0cd776ad4a40018050f46f","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -v '^[[:space:]]*#' backend/requirements.lock > scratch/req_body.txt && python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nbody = Path(\"scratch/req_body.txt\").read_text()\nheader = (\n    \"# Pinned install set for the backend (flask + gunicorn and the full\\n\"\n    \"# transitive closure, with hashes). Mirrors backend/requirements.lock,\\n\"\n    \"# which is used as the pip constraints file. Regenerate both together.\\n\"\n)\nPath(\"backend/requirements.txt\").write_text(header + body)\nprint((header + body)[:300])\nEOF","workdir":"/workspace"},"output":"# Pinned install set for the backend (flask + gunicorn and the full\n# transitive closure, with hashes). Mirrors backend/requirements.lock,\n# which is used as the pip constraints file. Regenerate both together.\nblinker==1.9.0 \\\n    --hash=sha256:b4ce2265a7abece45e7cc896e98dbebe6cead56bcf805a3d23136d1\n","metadata":{"output":"# Pinned install set for the backend (flask + gunicorn and the full\n# transitive closure, with hashes). Mirrors backend/requirements.lock,\n# which is used as the pip constraints file. Regenerate both together.\nblinker==1.9.0 \\\n    --hash=sha256:b4ce2265a7abece45e7cc896e98dbebe6cead56bcf805a3d23136d1\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -v '^[[:space:]]*#' backend/requirements.lock > scratch/req_body.txt && python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nbody = Path(\"scratch/req_body.txt\").read_text()\nheader = (\n    \"# Pinned install set for the backend (flask + gunicorn and the full\\n\"\n    \"# transitive closure, with hashes). Mirrors backend/requirements.lock,\\n\"\n    \"# which is used as the pip constraints file. Regenerate both together.\\n\"\n)\nPath(\"backend/requirements.txt\").write_text(header + body)\nprint((header + body)[:300])\nEOF","time":{"s